    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter June 4th with a clear emphasis on exploiting soft pitching matchups, headlined by **Trea Turner** (79.40) and **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (78.62), who both benefit from a prime encounter against a struggling arm. **Trea Turner** carries the day\u2019s highest reliability, bolstered by a 6.49 xERA opposing pitcher and the massive boost of batting second in a high-leverage environment. Meanwhile, **Pete Crow-Armstrong** remains a top priority; his elite speed profile\u2014essential for our scarcity-driven strategy\u2014combined with a favorable dynamic platoon advantage, makes him a must-start despite the moderate challenge of Ginn. **Kyle Schwarber** (78.21) and **Christian Yelich** (75.84) round out our premier tier, as both capitalize on the same soft pitching environment. **Christian Yelich** specifically overcomes a slight downgrade for facing an elite defensive catcher to maintain his elite efficiency score, primarily due to the 18% boost derived from facing Houser.\n\nOur most difficult roster decision today involved **Caleb Durbin** (58.56) and **Yordan Alvarez** (58.37), both of whom teetered on the edge of our starting threshold. While **Yordan Alvarez** possesses an elite .454 xwOBA, his score was suppressed by a difficult matchup against Jones, whereas **Caleb Durbin** benefited from the park and skill-based projections despite his lower batting order slot. Ultimately, we leaned into the favorable pitcher matchups for the starting eight, leaving our bench assets\u2014including **Junior Caminero**, **Colt Keith**, and minor-league stashes like **Hyeseong Kim** and **Rece Hinds**\u2014out of play due to off-days or roster status. Investors should keep a close eye on **Kazuma Okamoto** (46.54); while he maintains a start, he faces the stiffest test of the day against Sale, where his platoon edge is largely negated by the opponent\u2019s elite skill profile. Proceed with caution on the **Kazuma Okamoto** front, as any deviation in his confirmed order could push him below our 40-point floor.",
